// ONE IDENTITY ENROLLED 2026-08-25, and it carries a per-row reason because the nine rows this
// lane just examined do not, and that absence is what let a thrown claim be filed as a semantic
// red for weeks.
//
// THE CLASS: a call site spelling a name held by BOTH a local binding and a module-level free
// function reaches the FREE FUNCTION when the local's value is a reference to a named top-level
// function. Measured on a complete grid by two lanes independently -- let, parameter and pattern
// bindings all behave the same, and a local bound to a LAMBDA reaches the local -- so the binding
// form is not the axis and the value is. The collision is decided at the CALL SITE by the spelling
// used there: the same value handed to a differently-named parameter reaches the local, which is
// why a rename repairs it.
//
// WHY BELOW FLOOR RATHER THAN A NAMING HAZARD: where the shadowing symbol's arity DIFFERS the call
// refuses loudly, and where it AGREES a plausible wrong value is returned with no diagnostic.
// Reproduced twice on live corpus symbols before the fixture existed -- a displaced predicate
// returning a ParagraphBlock, and a fold over three elements answering 3 where the direct fold
// counts 2.
//
// THE ROW ASSERTS THE DESIRED LAW, not today's behaviour, so it reds now and greens on repair. Its
// three conjuncts return Bools and never throw, so this is an OBSERVED semantic red and never
// no-verdict debt.
//
// DISSOLUTION: it FLIPS TO A PERMANENT REGRESSION CONTROL when local bindings win, and is not
// deleted then. DESIGN 4b(4) -- a climb dissolves the lower-rung production machinery and KEEPS
// the discriminating evidence; deleting the probe on repair would recreate
// specification-without-execution one rung up. Its two green controls (the lambda column and the
// call-site rename) are already permanent for the same reason.
fn floor_expected_red_chunk_22() -> List<String> {
  Cons { head: "v2.test.claim.local_binding_shadow.local_named_function_binding_is_what_the_call_reaches", tail: Empty {} }
}

